[{"page": 1, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-1", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "T6. Carbon Nanorings", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 150.9783477783203, 230.20321655273438, 172.68597412109375]}, {"text": "7%", "bbox": [290.6499938964844, 193.6215057373047, 304.6280822753906, 207.18873596191406]}, {"text": "6.1", "bbox": [172.68299865722656, 209.5625, 186.7479705810547, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.2", "bbox": [204.3090057373047, 209.5625, 218.37399291992188, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.3", "bbox": [235.93499755859375, 209.5625, 249.99998474121094, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.4", "bbox": [267.5610046386719, 209.5625, 281.6259765625, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.5", "bbox": [299.18701171875, 209.5625, 313.2519836425781, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.6", "bbox": [330.81298828125, 209.5625, 344.8779602050781, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "6.7", "bbox": [362.4389953613281, 209.5625, 376.50396728515625, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "∑", "bbox": [405.1860046386719, 209.5625, 411.47100830078125, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "10", "bbox": [174.0189971923828, 225.50250244140625, 185.41400146484375, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "11", "bbox": [205.64500427246094, 225.50250244140625, 217.04000854492188, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [240.11900329589844, 225.50250244140625, 245.81539916992188, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "12", "bbox": [268.8970031738281, 225.50250244140625, 280.2919921875, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "24", "bbox": [300.52301025390625, 225.50250244140625, 311.9179992675781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "20", "bbox": [332.14898681640625, 225.50250244140625, 343.5439758300781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [366.62298583984375, 225.50250244140625, 372.3193664550781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "83", "bbox": [402.6319885253906, 225.50250244140625, 414.0269775390625, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "In 2019, C18, the first example of a new class of carbon allotropes called cyclo[n]carbons (C𝑛) was de-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 249.4652099609375, 538.5745849609375, 280.5965576171875]}, {"text": "tected. Cyclocarbons are monocyclic, all-carbon compounds with high strain energy and low stability.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 271.28851318359375, 538.5846557617188, 284.8557434082031]}, {"text": "They can be generated and analysed by bond-resolved Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM). Cyclocarbons", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 283.2434997558594, 538.5640869140625, 296.81072998046875]}, {"text": "have interesting aromatic properties based on their π systems. C13 has triplet (3C13, spin S = 1), and", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 280.335205078125, 538.5785522460938, 312.73773193359375]}, {"text": "singlet (1C13, spin S = 0) forms.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 293.9571838378906, 200.2569122314453, 326.0678405761719]}, {"text": "6.1", "bbox": [78.60799407958984, 333.2664794921875, 92.84233093261719, 346.8337097167969]}, {"text": "Based on Hückel’s rule, fill in the table with the number of distinct aromatic (A)", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 333.2664794921875, 480.5848388671875, 346.833740234375]}, {"text": "and anti-aromatic (AA) 𝜋-systems present in each of C18, C16, 3C13, and 1C13.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 331.2522277832031, 480.5846252441406, 367.2721252441406]}, {"text": "Fill in all blanks.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 359.552490234375, 194.5926055908203, 373.1197204589844]}, {"text": "10.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 333.1914978027344, 526.921142578125, 346.75872802734375]}, {"text": "Later, cyclo[n]carbons C10, C12, C14, C20, and C26 were generated by a combination of dehalogenation", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 386.98150634765625, 538.5604248046875, 403.03973388671875]}, {"text": "and retro-Bergman (1) reactions on a surface. AFM images taken during the synthesis of C14 are shown", "bbox": [56.69300842285156, 398.9364929199219, 538.5792846679688, 414.9947204589844]}, {"text": "below:", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 410.8914794921875, 87.44817352294922, 424.4587097167969]}, {"text": "6.2", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 701.9124755859375, 92.84233856201172, 715.4796752929688]}, {"text": "Draw structures B-D. Note they may contain one or more unpaired electrons.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 701.9124755859375, 480.59393310546875, 715.4796752929688]}, {"text": "The structure of A is given as an example.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 713.8674926757812, 309.9571533203125, 727.4346923828125]}, {"text": "11.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 701.8364868164062, 526.921142578125, 715.4036865234375]}]}, {"page": 2, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-2", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "6.3", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "The voltages applied during the AFM-mediated synthesis of C𝑛may vary. Us-", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 156.3612060546875, 480.5843505859375, 187.4925537109375]}, {"text": "ing the given C–X bond energies, choose the possible halogen(s) in the halo-", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 178.18450927734375, 480.5812683105469, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "genated reagent for C18 synthesis via a retro-Bergman reaction with a voltage", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 190.1405029296875, 480.5830993652344, 206.19773864746094]}, {"text": "of 2.5 V acting on the electrons.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 202.0955047607422, 261.9289245605469, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "Bond", "bbox": [215.03399658203125, 231.67649841308594, 239.8232879638672, 245.2437286376953]}, {"text": "(C–X)", "bbox": [215.88499450683594, 243.63150024414062, 238.97634887695312, 257.19873046875]}, {"text": "Bond Dissociation Energy /", "bbox": [259.3330078125, 230.9355010986328, 384.88238525390625, 244.5027313232422]}, {"text": "kJ mol−1", "bbox": [302.03900146484375, 219.55413818359375, 341.6832275390625, 285.5065612792969]}, {"text": "C–F", "bbox": [219.2050018310547, 260.3125, 235.65367126464844, 273.8797302246094]}, {"text": "467", "bbox": [313.56597900390625, 260.3125, 330.6595764160156, 273.8797302246094]}, {"text": "C–Cl", "bbox": [217.35899353027344, 276.25250244140625, 237.50148010253906, 289.8197326660156]}, {"text": "346", "bbox": [313.56597900390625, 276.25250244140625, 330.6595764160156, 289.8197326660156]}, {"text": "C–Br", "bbox": [216.4949951171875, 292.1925048828125, 238.36373901367188, 305.7597351074219]}, {"text": "290", "bbox": [313.56597900390625, 292.1925048828125, 330.6595764160156, 305.7597351074219]}, {"text": "C–I", "bbox": [220.1020050048828, 308.13348388671875, 234.75564575195312, 321.7007141113281]}, {"text": "228", "bbox": [313.56597900390625, 308.13348388671875, 330.6595764160156, 321.7007141113281]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}, {"text": "In 2025, the first relatively stable cyclo[48]carbon was synthesised. The molecule was stabilised by cate-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 354.66448974609375, 538.6016235351562, 368.2317199707031]}, {"text": "nation (forming interlocking rings) with macrocycle E and was first characterised by electrospray mass", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 366.6204833984375, 538.5740966796875, 380.1877136230469]}, {"text": "spectrometry in positive mode.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 378.5754699707031, 201.94837951660156, 392.1427001953125]}, {"text": "6.4", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 594.2144775390625, 92.84233856201172, 607.7816772460938]}, {"text": "In the mass spectrum obtained, four intense peaks were observed m/z: 591,", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 594.2144775390625, 480.5869140625, 607.7816772460938]}, {"text": "783, 879, and 1174. Suggest the identity of these ions. Use integer atomic", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 606.1694946289062, 480.5853576660156, 619.7366943359375]}, {"text": "masses and assume no fragmentation happened. The ion corresponding to", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 620.469482421875, 480.5472717285156, 634.0366821289062]}, {"text": "m/z = 591 is given as an example.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 632.4244995117188, 270.1251525878906, 645.99169921875]}, {"text": "12.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 594.1384887695312, 526.921142578125, 607.7056884765625]}]}, {"page": 3, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-3", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Cycloparaphenylene (CPP) is another cyclic, highly-strained molecule commonly called a carbon", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5955200195312, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "nanohoop. The synthesis of the smallest known member, [5]CPP, is shown below, where PhI(OAc)2 acts", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 152.25897216796875, 538.5836181640625, 186.84912109375]}, {"text": "as a two electron oxidant.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 179.12950134277344, 176.75296020507812, 192.6967315673828]}, {"text": "(equiv. = Equivalent, excess = Excess)", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 617.5349731445312, 228.18240356445312, 652.1251220703125]}, {"text": "6.5", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 655.41552734375, 92.84233856201172, 668.9827270507812]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of F-L.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 655.41552734375, 241.20362854003906, 668.9827270507812]}, {"text": "24.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1519775390625, 655.3395385742188, 526.921142578125, 668.90673828125]}]}, {"page": 4, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-4", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Next generation nanobelts were constructed from porphyrin rings and triple bonds using the template", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5537109375, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "synthesis method. Hint: M is the thermodynamic product and has four types of protons.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 167.17449951171875, 467.60308837890625, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "(equiv. = Equivalent)", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 617.0269775390625, 150.54385375976562, 651.6171264648438]}, {"text": "6.6", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 654.9075317382812, 92.84233856201172, 668.4747314453125]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of M-R.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 654.9075317382812, 246.07862854003906, 668.4747314453125]}, {"text": "20.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1519775390625, 654.83251953125, 526.921142578125, 668.3997192382812]}]}, {"page": 5, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q6-5", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "When aromatic rings are joined to form a macrocycle, oxidation or reduction can produce global aro-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5718383789062, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "maticity, in which π electrons are delocalised around the entire macrocycle. Only the π system forming", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 167.17449951171875, 538.5863647460938, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "the continuous conjugated pathway around the ring participates in this delocalisation. As an example,", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 179.12950134277344, 538.57470703125, 192.6967315673828]}, {"text": "[n]CPPs can become globally aromatic upon addition or removal of electrons. The number of π electrons", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 191.0854949951172, 538.5640258789062, 204.65272521972656]}, {"text": "is counted only along the bold pathway shown below.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 203.04049682617188, 307.1135559082031, 216.60772705078125]}, {"text": "When P6 is oxidised, it can exhibit global aromaticity and global anti-aromaticity.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 291.5115051269531, 432.7892150878906, 305.0787353515625]}, {"text": "6.7", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 314.47650146484375, 92.84233856201172, 328.0437316894531]}, {"text": "Based on Hückel’s rule, find the minimum number of electrons, n(e), from P6", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 314.47650146484375, 480.58489990234375, 328.0437316894531]}, {"text": "that should be removed to achieve global aromaticity. Write the total number", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 326.4314880371094, 480.5758056640625, 339.99871826171875]}, {"text": "of π electrons, n(t), in the global aromatic system.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 338.386474609375, 345.709228515625, 351.9537048339844]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 314.4004821777344, 521.8194580078125, 327.96771240234375]}]}]